A||||22||rodmcneill||Good brand of battery?||||5||
Z||000000||rodmcneill||08-26-2001||11:14 PM||||I need to buy a new battery for one of my Fiero's this week. Probably a midrange battery, any suggestions on best battery for the buck? I see Sam's Club sells Champion brand, good or bad? just buy a Die-Hard?. Are Interstate batteries any good?||||reg||5
Z||000001||artherd||08-26-2001||11:22 PM||||The Optima spiral cells are the best battery going.<P>Exide makes a cheaper knock-off I belive.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rodmcneill:<BR><B>I need to buy a new battery for one of my Fiero's this week. Probably a midrange battery, any suggestions on best battery for the buck? I see Sam's Club sells Champion brand, good or bad? just buy a Die-Hard?. Are Interstate batteries any good?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000002||mrfiero||08-26-2001||11:24 PM||||Die-Hard is a good choice.  I have a Delco replacement in my GT.....it's almost identical to the original equipment one.<P>Interstate batteries aren't too bad......I have no experience with Champion, so I can't help you there.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Joe Torma||08-26-2001||11:25 PM||||Get an Optima.  They are good for 900 starts and will turn over any engine easily.||||reg||1
Z||000004||stimpy||08-26-2001||11:29 PM||||I have the Exide "knock off"- the Orbital. I think it's freakin brilliant. Retails for $120, but I got mine at wholesale list price ($80) by going to the local distributor.  The spiral core batteries like the Orbital and the Optima are fantastic for a hot environment like the Fiero, as they WILL NOT LEAK. Ever. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||2birds||08-26-2001||11:43 PM||||Lead-acid batteries are pretty much the same.  Pb+Pb02+2H2SO4&lt;=&gt;2PbSO4+2H20+electrons<BR>There are only a few manufacturers, too.<P>I'd stick with someone that haas a decent warranty (stores everywhere) in case you are somewhere and your battery fails, but the Interstate dealers are all closed, the nearest Sears in an hour away, etc.  Wal-mart is everywhere, but my nearest Sears is an hour away.  I used to have a Wards battery, but they didn't exist where I lived in the Pac Northwest, so I was SOL when it died.<BR>I can't see the reason for buying something like an Optima.  Just my opinion, though. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||rodmcneill||08-27-2001||12:07 AM||||I saw Sears has a newer battery,top of the line. Sells for about $150.00. Has some kind of circuit in it that prevents battery drain,also comes with a remote that you can disable the battery with to prevent theft. Anyone have any experience with this one?||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||08-27-2001||08:35 AM||||the optima is a gell cell... the orbital is a dry cell. the dry is better. i've got one.. had an optima in my SE the orbital is lighter and has a warranty. got mine for Christmas.. "stocking streacher"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>Orbital available at NAPA.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Kasdan||08-27-2001||09:11 AM||||Just go with a DieHard Gold series...works great, i use them in all my vehicles<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan<BR>1986 GT Fastback, <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FIERO2.JPG">       <BR>Holley Ram-Air, Power Steering, K&N Filtercharger, Bosch Wires, Bosch Platinum Plugs, Conrad Distribuiter Cap/Rotor, New GT Seats, New Headliner, New Carpet, Ocelet Exhaust, Red Underbody Light Kit (coming soon)<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000009||LarryB||08-27-2001||11:24 AM||||I've used most of the names mentioned above, they've all been fine with 1 exception: Champion. 1 let go after about 8 months, the other after a year. I got the warranty honored, but its still a PITA.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>||||reg||8
Z||000010||Nashco||08-27-2001||11:38 AM||||I'm a very big suppporter of Optima batteries...I've got a very impressive testimonial story to tell you, but I'll spare some time and bandwidth; OPTIMAS ARE GREAT!  I've had bad experience with Champion and Die-Hard.  If you're tight on cash, go with Interstate, but if you can afford the 110 bucks, get an optima, it's the best buy you'll ever make on a battery!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000011||theogre||08-27-2001||07:12 PM||||There are very few companies that actually make batteries in the U.S. You want to find out who really made it if you can. Most large chain batteries are this way. <P>Diehard security battery listed above is made by Johnson Controls for Sears. Just who makes the rest of Sears batteries can vary depending on who has the contract... I think that is also Johnson but I couldn't say for sure.<P>I have a Wall-mart battery in mine now. been there around 2 years. I forgot who made it. Exide or Johnson Control.<P>Interstate was always decent when we used them in NY... I haven't used them in a long time only becuase there's no handy outlet for them near me.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Kasdan||08-27-2001||08:20 PM||||My current Die-Hard has a SEVEN year warranty....<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan<BR>1986 GT Fastback, <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FIERO2.JPG">       <BR>Holley Ram-Air, Power Steering, K&N Filtercharger, Bosch Wires, Bosch Platinum Plugs, Conrad Distribuiter Cap/Rotor, New GT Seats, New Headliner, New Carpet, Ocelet Exhaust, Red Underbody Light Kit (coming soon)<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000013||PBJ||08-27-2001||08:24 PM||||I would only put in a true "maintance free" battery, these do not have pop off tops and do not rott the metal around because of the maintance free system-they do not went like others.  sooo buy a GM ACDELCO battery.  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forsalestart.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||varnster||08-27-2001||09:42 PM||||I just got a champion vortex gell cell, 3 year replacement 8 year prorate. I picked it<BR>cause its the same color red as the engine.<BR>Its about $130 US. I have heard good things <BR>about this battery, but havent used it long <BR>enough to give the old stamp of approval. ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Loki||08-27-2001||10:15 PM||||DO NOT!!! I REPEAT DO NOT!!! Buy ProStart from Pep-Boys, I see sooo many come back not even a month old...Piece of ****  battery<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki-mg/loki_sig.jpg">  <BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>http://members.home.net/loki-mg||||reg||1
Z||000016||samoht||08-27-2001||10:19 PM||||i work at sears so i have to go with the Die Hard .. I am partial though...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||RossT||08-28-2001||02:39 AM||||Follow this link to a picture of the optima battery in my fiero.  The redtop comes in a smaller size that fits nicely.  got mine at<BR>interstate batteries.  Very happy with it and no longer need to worry about leaking acid.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000002/HTML/20010706-1-005058.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000002/HTML/20010706-1-005058.html</A> <p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 08-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||Nashco||08-28-2001||03:26 AM||||You can see my testimonial at the bottom of the page linked above.  I now have that battery in Dad's K-5 Blazer, going like brand new.  It can sit for weeks, and when you go to start it, it fires right up.  Charges fast if it's ever needed (had to do it once after running 10 days without a generator), doesn't emit metal-eating chemicals, can be oriented in any position (upside down, sideways, etc. for front end transfers), and has dual posts incase you ever want to use it in another vehicle with top posts!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000019||artherd||08-28-2001||05:40 PM||||Hey Trav, I have the Orbital in one of my cars actually, and I LOVE it!!  I have the blue-top deep cycle version, it's bloody great, just like the Optimas.  Lighter though, I think I have a new favourite...<P>They are at NAPA, and  <P>I'll never buy a 'normal' battery again, spiral would rules.<P>I did once see a demo of the Optimas, where they took a hacksaw to one under load....  it fuses itself closed with a minimum of protest, dosen't explode or even drip, rock on!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000020||Rick 88||08-28-2001||05:49 PM||||If you are on a budget, the AutoZone battery seems to hold up well. I replaced my AC Delco which was leaking from the terminals. So much for a sealed battery. I also installed a battery mat and terminal washers to help neutralize any battery acid. <P>Rick ||||reg||1
Z||000021||Jinx||08-28-2001||08:06 PM||||go with the Die-Hard||||reg||14
Z||000022||1FST2M6||08-29-2001||08:22 AM||||after seeing what a normal battery (die-hard what ever) can do or does do to your car i'm sure everyone would be like artherd and myself. Gell cell or Dry cell all the way.<P>how many of you have actually removed the battery and poured baking soda don the battery area? i'd bet not many.. the acid from a wet cell  eats the frame away and can cause failure of the battery tray, rusting of the frame itself and it's REALLY difficult to make look nice. ||||reg||1
